{"seconds": 27.5, "exit": 0, "final": "Excellent! The main line is clear: **Qxc3+ Kxc3 Rxc2+ Kd3 Rxc1**, winning White's rook. This is a classic **fork and follow-up** pattern\u2014the queen checks and forces the king to capture, then the rook delivers a discovered check with a fork on the rook.\n\n**Coaching note:** Your queen check on c3 is not just about trading queens\u2014it's a trap! After White's king captures, your rook swoops to c2 with check, forking the king and rook. The key lesson: when your opponent's pieces are on the same line (c-file), look for ways to attack multiple pieces with forcing moves like checks.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qxc3+\", \"line\": [\"Qxc3+\", \"Kxc3\", \"Rxc2+\", \"Kd3\", \"Rxc1\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "6k1/1p3ppp/2q1p3/3pP3/bP1P4/2Q2NP1/r1PK1P1P/2R5 b - - 4 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "6k1/1p3ppp/2q1p3/3pP3/bP1P4/2Q2NP1/r1PK1P1P/2R5 b - - 4 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "6k1/1p3ppp/2q1p3/3pP3/bP1P4/2Q2NP1/r1PK1P1P/2R5 b - - 4 21"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "6k1/1p3ppp/2q1p3/3pP3/bP1P4/2Q2NP1/r1PK1P1P/2R5 b - - 4 21", "move": "Qxc3+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "6k1/1p3ppp/2q1p3/3pP3/bP1P4/2Q2NP1/r1PK1P1P/2R5 b - - 4 21", "move": "Rxc2+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "6k1/1p3ppp/4p3/3pP3/bP1P4/2q2NP1/r1PK1P1P/2R5 w - - 0 22", "move": "Kxc3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "6k1/1p3ppp/4p3/3pP3/bP1P4/2q2NP1/r1PK1P1P/2R5 w - - 0 22", "move": "Ke2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "6k1/1p3ppp/4p3/3pP3/bP1P4/2q2NP1/r1PK1P1P/2R5 w - - 0 22", "move": "Kd1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "6k1/1p3ppp/4p3/3pP3/bP1P4/2K2NP1/r1P2P1P/2R5 b - - 0 22", "move": "Ra3+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "6k